## 🚀 Local Development Setup

### Step 1: Clone the Repository
Open **PowerShell** or **Windows Terminal** and run:
```powershell
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/crimetrake.git
cd crimetrake_project
```

### Step 2: Create Virtual Environment
```powershell
# Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# Activate virtual environment
venv\Scripts\activate
```

You should now see `(venv)` at the start of your terminal prompt.

> ⚠️ **If activation is blocked by PowerShell**, run this first:
> ```powershell
> Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope CurrentUser -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned
> ```
> Then re-run `venv\Scripts\activate`.

### Step 3: Install Dependencies

#### Basic Installation (Without Face Recognition)
```powershell
pip install Django==4.2.7
pip install pillow==10.1.0
pip install scikit-learn==1.3.2
pip install pandas==2.1.3
pip install numpy==1.26.2
```

#### Full Installation (With Face Recognition)

> ⚠️ Installing `dlib` on Windows requires extra steps. Follow carefully.

**Step A — Install Visual Studio Build Tools:**
1. Download from [Visual Studio Build Tools](https://visualstudio.microsoft.com/visual-cpp-build-tools/)
2. Run the installer
3. Select **"Desktop development with C++"**
4. Click Install

**Step B — Install CMake:**
1. Download from [cmake.org](https://cmake.org/download/)
2. Run the installer
3. ✅ Select **"Add CMake to system PATH for all users"**

**Step C — Install dlib using a pre-built wheel (Easiest method):**
1. Go to [https://github.com/sachadee/Dlib](https://github.com/sachadee/Dlib)
2. Download the `.whl` file matching your Python version (e.g., `dlib-19.24.1-cp311-cp311-win_amd64.whl` for Python 3.11)
3. Install it:
```powershell
pip install path\to\downloaded\dlib-xx-win_amd64.whl
```

**Step D — Install remaining requirements:**
```powershell
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

> ℹ️ If face recognition installation fails, the app will still work — you'll just see a warning message on startup.

