## 🐛 Troubleshooting (Windows 11)

### ❌ "No module named 'django'"
Virtual environment is not activated. Run:
```powershell
venv\Scripts\activate
pip install Django==4.2.7
```

### ❌ PowerShell blocks script execution
```powershell
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope CurrentUser -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned
```

### ❌ Pillow not installed (ImageField error)
```powershell
python -m pip install Pillow
```

### ❌ dlib installation failed
Use the pre-built wheel method described in [Step 3](#step-3-install-dependencies). The app works without face recognition if needed.

### ❌ "CSRF verification failed"
Clear your browser cache and cookies, then try again.

### ❌ Static files not loading
```powershell
python manage.py collectstatic
```

### ❌ Database migration errors
```powershell
# Delete all migration files (keep __init__.py)
Get-ChildItem -Recurse -Filter "*.py" -Path "*/migrations" | Where-Object { $_.Name -ne "__init__.py" } | Remove-Item

# Recreate migrations
python manage.py makemigrations
python manage.py migrate
```

### ❌ Port 8000 already in use
```powershell
# Find the process using port 8000
netstat -ano | findstr :8000

# Kill the process (replace <PID> with the actual number)
taskkill /PID <PID> /F
```

